{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.LengthAdditive"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.length_sortPerm_mul_eq_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.length_sortPerm_mul_eq_add","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L194-L212","doc":"**The mirror length identity**: `ℓ(d · w) = ℓ(d) + ℓ(w)` for `w` in the Young\nsubgroup of `c'`.\n\nTogether with `length_mul_sortPerm_eq_add` this gives `Tw_mul_Tw` its hypothesis on\nboth sides, which is what the two-sided `m_{st}` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.index_eq_of_mem_invSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.index_eq_of_mem_invSet","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L175-L192","doc":"**A Young element inverts only inside a block.**  Across two blocks the order is\nfixed by the block order, so no inversion can straddle them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.length_mul_sortPerm_eq_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.length_mul_sortPerm_eq_add","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L150-L162","doc":"**`sortPerm` is minimal-length in its coset** — Mathas' `d ∈ D_μ` — given that it\nis increasing inside each block of `c'`.\n\n**Unconditional**, and now a one-line corollary of Proposition 3.3 above: the only\nproperty of `sortPerm` it ever used is that it is distinguished.\n\nThe conclusion is what `T_v T_d = T_{vd}` needs, and hence what the intertwining\n`T_d · x_μ = x_ν · T_d` runs on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.length_mul_eq_add_of_isDistinguished","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.length_mul_eq_add_of_isDistinguished","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L121-L148","doc":"**Proposition 3.3, length half.**  `ℓ(w·d) = ℓ(w) + ℓ(d)` for `w ∈ S_μ` and any\n`d ∈ D_μ`.\n\nThis is what gives `T_{wd} = T_w T_d` through `TwBasis.Tw_mul_Tw`, and it is the fact\nMathas' whole coset bookkeeping runs on.  `length_mul_sortPerm_eq_add` is the `d =\nsortPerm` case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.sortPerm_isDistinguished","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.sortPerm_isDistinguished","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L113-L119","doc":"`sortPerm` is distinguished — which is why the specialised proofs above worked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.IsDistinguished","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.IsDistinguished","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L105-L111","doc":"**Mathas' `D_μ`**: the permutations that never invert two labels landing in the same\nblock of `c`.\n\nTableau-side this is \"`t^μ d` is row standard\"; stated here as the order condition it\namounts to, since the rows of `t^μ` are `c`'s blocks in order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.sortPerm_strictMono_within","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.sortPerm_strictMono_within","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L74-L87","doc":"**`sortPerm` is increasing inside each block** — it permutes the *rows*, keeping\neach row's own order, which is how Mathas specifies `d`.\n\nBoth labels get the same block start and the same source offset base, so the\ncomparison reduces to the labels themselves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.coe_sortPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.coe_sortPerm","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L63-L72","doc":"The **value** of `sortPerm m l`: the start of its target block, plus its offset\ninside its source block.\n\nBoth halves are Mathlib's (`coe_embedding`, `coe_invEmbedding`); `finCongr` does not\nmove a value, so the size-matching cast is invisible here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.index_apply_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.index_apply_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L57-L61","doc":"A Young element does not move a label out of its block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.index_sortPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.index_sortPerm","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L51-L55","doc":"The block index of `sortPerm m l`, in the direct form the argument below uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.lt_of_index_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMinimal.lt_of_index_lt","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMinimal.lean#L38-L49","doc":"**Blocks of a composition are consecutive**: a smaller block index means a strictly\nsmaller position.\n\nAssembled from `sizeUpTo_index_le`, `lt_sizeUpTo_index_succ` and `monotone_sizeUpTo`;\nMathlib has the three bounds but not this consequence. ","signatureChunk":0}]}